# What never enters the Docker build context.
#
# The builder stage compiles dist/ and web/dist/ from the source in the
# context (2026-10-18: four production deploys shipped a dist built hours
# earlier while the image label carried the new git revision). Keeping the
# host's own build outputs OUT of the context is half of that fix: a stale
# local dist/ can neither be COPYed nor sit in the context pretending to be
# current, and `COPY dist/ …` fails loudly instead of shipping old code.
#
# Keep this aligned with .teployignore (what `teploy deploy` syncs) —
# scripts/check-image-sources.mjs fails CI when the two drift apart.
.git
.github
.forgejo
_internal
docs
evals
examples
images
reference
swebench
node_modules
web/node_modules
dist
web/dist
deploy/vendor
*.log
ship-secrets.env
*.secrets.env
teploy.yml
teploy.install.yml
